From e74ab064f8a326a6397e87db5da698337ced04fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viktor Semenov <suit.uanic@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:21:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/45] Send players and player-coloured templates in the
 Specula feed

Feed format v4. Template records gain a flags byte; flag 1 says the
template's minimap colour is its owner's player colour (no
Minimap/Color, as CCmpMinimap::Init decides). A new players record
gives each player's name, colour, team, state and stance towards every
other player, read from GuiInterface.GetSimulationState like the
session GUI does. It is sampled every 5 turns and written only when it
changes, so viewers can show diplomacy colours themselves.
